             </property>
             <property name="bottomMargin">
              <number>0</number>
             </property>
             <item>
              <widget class="QLabel" name="methods_label">
               <property name="text">
                <string>&lt;b&gt;Filter:&lt;/b&gt; the selected channels are filtered between 0.3 and 62 Hz (Butterworth band-pass, order 6, zero phase) before the analysis.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Spectrum (Welch [1]):&lt;/b&gt; the signal is divided into windows (Hann window) and a Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) is applied to each window. The periodograms of the windows are averaged per sleep stage and over the whole recording. The frequency bin resolution is 1 / window length (s): 0.2 Hz with 5 s windows. The power of the bins is summed in each 1 Hz band, from the first to the last frequency.</string>
               </property>
               <property name="textFormat">
                <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
               </property>
               <property name="wordWrap">
                <bool>true</bool>
               </property>
               <property name="variant" stdset="0">
                <string notr="true">help</string>
               </property>
              </widget>
             </item>
